Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:55:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1031/1259] Viktor's stable sampling as the defaults; the
 wanted key follows a new plan

- Engine and page: score planner 0.95 / 0.95 / 50, music 0.9 / 0.95 / 100 with penalty 1.3
  over 100 tokens, guidance 1.6 in every mode (the release: 0.7 / 0.9 / 30, 1.0 / 0.95 / 100,
  1.2 over 50, guidance 1.0, 1.01 in Direct). The shape sliders are re-centred on them; the
  tips name the new default and the release one. A take whose request left guidance to the
  engine says "default", not a number it cannot know.
- The wanted key (1019) moved a score only when the form had none: a new plan over an old
  score stayed in its own key (Viktor: B-flat minor wanted, E minor came). A score is new when
  its notes are; a transposition or a hand edit of K: is not. A move from the score drawer
  becomes the wanted key, so the watcher does not undo it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
